{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Even","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.StarOrdered","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity","lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.ChiralFermionBraidWords"],"declarations":46,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.h2_two_feasible_one_not","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.h2_two_feasible_one_not","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L285-L290","doc":"`σ₀²`, the shipped gluon vertex, is PSD-feasible; `σ₀` is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.h2_psdFeasible_iff_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.h2_psdFeasible_iff_even","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L270-L283","doc":"**The abstract predicate recovers the proved parity rule.** For `0 < q`,\n`σ₀^k` is PSD-feasible in the sense of `SDPSelected` iff `k` is even —\n`QOU.QBeta.GluonVertexPsdParity.vertex_psd_iff_even`, re-derived through\n`Matrix.PosSemidef` on the two blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.h2Blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.h2Blocks","kind":"def","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L265-L268","doc":"The two `H₂` blocks (`true` = symmetric `(2)`, `false` = alternating\n`(1,1)`), on candidates `k ↦ σ₀^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.cost_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.cost_eq","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L244-L250","doc":"Two SDP-selected words have equal cost: selection is unique up to cost\nties. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.minimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.minimal","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L242-L242","doc":"`w` minimises the cost over PSD-feasible candidates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.psd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.psd","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L240-L240","doc":"Every Wedderburn projection of `w` is PSD. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.mem","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L238-L238","doc":"`w` is one of the candidates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected.mk","kind":"ctor","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L235-L235","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.SDPSelected","kind":"structure","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L232-L242","doc":"**SDP selection.** `w` is the canonical word for a candidate set `cands`\nand cost `cost` iff it is a candidate, it is PSD-feasible, and no PSD-feasible\ncandidate has smaller cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks.PSDFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks.PSDFeasible","kind":"def","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L226-L230","doc":"**PSD feasibility**: every Wedderburn projection of `w` is positive\nsemidefinite. This is constraint (1)+(2) of `prop:confinement-sdp` read on a\ncandidate word, with the actual `Matrix.PosSemidef` cone — not a placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks.proj","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L221-L221","doc":"The block projections `π_l : W → Mat_{d l}(R)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks.mk","kind":"ctor","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.WedderburnBlocks","kind":"structure","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L216-L221","doc":"**Wedderburn block data** for a candidate type `W`: for each block label\n`l : ι` of dimension `d l`, the matrix image of each candidate under the\nblock projection `π_l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.toCorpus_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.toCorpus_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L207-L210","doc":"This file's `borromean` is the corpus's `borromean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.toCorpus_vertex_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.toCorpus_vertex_zero","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L202-L205","doc":"`vertex 0` is the corpus's `gluonUnit = σ₀σ₁⁻¹ = [1, -2]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.toCorpus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.toCorpus","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L197-L200","doc":"Translate to the corpus encoding of `QOU.StandardModel.BraidWords`\n(entry `±(i+1)` for `σᵢ^{±1}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.borromean_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.borromean_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L194-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.borromean_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.borromean_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L190-L192","doc":"`β_Bor` is γγ-produced: three pair-production events. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.borromean","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L186-L188","doc":"`β_Bor = (σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`, written as the nested product the `GammaGammaWord`\nconstructors produce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_single","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L176-L180","doc":"A single positive crossing has alternating character `−q⁻¹` — nonzero, so\nthe template `pp` bond is likewise not in the Gram's range, but for a\ndifferent reason than a γγ-word (it is not a unit of the character). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L169-L174","doc":"Hence it never vanishes: no γγ-produced word is killed by the alternating\nblock, which is what the D-frame Frobenius rows would require. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L162-L167","doc":"**The alternating character of every γγ-produced word is `1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_vertex","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L158-L160","doc":"One pair-production vertex has alternating character `(−q⁻¹)(−q) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar_append","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L154-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.altChar","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L145-L152","doc":"The one-dimensional **alternating** representation of the Hecke algebra,\n`σᵢ ↦ −q⁻¹` (and so `σᵢ⁻¹ ↦ −q`), evaluated on a word. Under convention D the\ntrace-form radical of `H₃(q)` is spanned by `v_k = (−1/q)^{len b_k}` — the\nalternating character of the normal-form basis — so this is the functional\nwhose vanishing decides whether a word's normal form lies in the range of\nthe Gram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.not_gammaGamma_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.not_gammaGamma_single","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L131-L137","doc":"A single positive crossing has writhe `1`, hence is **not** γγ-produced.\nIn particular the template inter-nucleon `pp` bond `σ₀` is not, on its own, a\npair-production word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.length_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.length_even","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L123-L129","doc":"**Every γγ-produced word has an even number of crossings.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.length_vertex_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.length_vertex_append","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L119-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L113-L117","doc":"**Every γγ-produced word has writhe `0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe_vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe_vertex","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L109-L111","doc":"One vertex pairs a positive with a negative crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe_append","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L106-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.writhe","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Writhe: the sum of the crossing signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.sign","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L100-L101","doc":"Sign of a crossing, `±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.GammaGammaWord.cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.GammaGammaWord.cons","kind":"ctor","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L98-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.GammaGammaWord.nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.GammaGammaWord.nil","kind":"ctor","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L97-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.GammaGammaWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.GammaGammaWord","kind":"inductive","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L94-L98","doc":"**γγ-produced words**: the words that are (left-to-right) products of\npair-production vertices. The empty word is the empty product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.vertex","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L89-L92","doc":"The pair-production vertex `σᵢ σᵢ₊₁⁻¹` — one photon on strands `(i, i+1)`\nand one anti-photon on `(i+1, i+2)`, the `γγ̄` factor of\n`gamma_gamma_pair_production_decomposition.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Word","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L86-L87","doc":"A braid word is a list of crossings; `[]` is the identity braid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instReprCrossing.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instReprCrossing.repr","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instReprCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instReprCrossing","kind":"instance","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instDecidableEqCrossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instDecidableEqCrossing","kind":"instance","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instDecidableEqCrossing.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.instDecidableEqCrossing.decEq","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing.pos","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L83-L83","doc":"`true` = positive crossing `σᵢ`, `false` = `σᵢ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing.gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing.gen","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Generator index `i` of `σᵢ`, 0-based. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing.mk","kind":"ctor","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection.Crossing","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaWordSelection.lean#L77-L84","doc":"A crossing: which Artin generator `σ_gen` (0-based) and its sign\n(`pos = true` for `σ_gen`, `false` for `σ_gen⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}